# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Borg — .gitignore
#
# Denylist style: most files are tracked by default; this file
# lists what to keep out. When you add a new kind of sensitive
# file, add a rule here BEFORE the first `git add`.
# Verify with:  git check-ignore -v <path>
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Backups & temp scratch ───────────────────────────────────
*_bak_*
*.bak
*.orig
.tmp.*
**/.tmp.*

# ── Log and state directories (anywhere in the tree) ───────────────────
**/logs/
**/log/
**/state/

# ── Secrets / local config ───────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# …but committed *.example templates carry keys + docs, never values
# (e.g. .bin/email-shared.env.example). Re-allow them past the .env.* rule.
!**/.env.example
!**/*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*_token*
*_secret*
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/.credentials*
# Private rules — machine/infrastructure-specific guidance the agent should load
# locally but never publish (e.g. host addresses, mount paths). Still loaded by
# the harness (they end in .md); just kept out of this public repo. Same
# `.local.` convention as settings.local.json above.
**/.claude/rules/*.local.md

# Per-agent confidential context and Claude Code's local instruction loader.
# Public synthetic templates use `.private.example/` and remain tracked. This
# also covers the private scheduled-task tables at `.private/scheduled-tasks/`,
# whose local job identities must never enter the public repository.
**/.private/
**/CLAUDE.local.md

# Allow shared Claude settings, scheduled jobs, etc. — only the
# `*.local.json` variants and credential files are ignored above.

# ── Obsidian workspace state (per-machine) ───────────────────
.obsidian/
#**/.obsidian/workspace*
#**/.obsidian/cache
#**/.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# ── vinny (privileged legal / contract material) ─────────────
# No rule needed: the generic scaffold is tracked like any other agent's, and
# every matter document, draft, and strategy note lives under `vinny/.private/`,
# already ignored by the `**/.private/` rule above.

# ── warren-bot-fett (financial / portfolio) ──────────────────
warren-bot-fett/PORTFOLIO.md

# ── mrs-beast (personal social identity) ─────────────────────
mrs-beast/.claude/commands/*-image-prompt.md
mrs-beast/.claude/scheduled/*-image-prompt.prompt
mrs-beast/.claude/scheduled/last30days-raw/

# ── cerebruh (second-brain content) ──────────────────────────
# Track structure + templates + the index, ignore actual notes.
cerebruh/ingest/*
!cerebruh/ingest/.gitkeep
cerebruh/wikis/*
!cerebruh/wikis/.gitkeep

# ── architetto (initialized product repos) ───────────────────
# Each repo under repos/ is its own independent git repo and is NOT
# part of The Borg's history. Track the directory's existence only.
repos/*
!repos/.gitkeep

# ── Shared scratch space (agent working files) ────────────────
# Any agent's temporary/working files go here, not scattered across the tree.
# Track the directory's existence only, ignore its contents.
tmp/*
!tmp/.gitkeep

# Defense in depth: agent-local scratch directories violate the shared-tmp rule,
# but ignore their contents if one is accidentally created so they cannot leak.
/*/tmp/

# ── Generic catch-alls for accidental drops ──────────────────
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.log
node_modules/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
